From 5ec9e93d23d78dfa886d3d3a9934ccf432d04269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:34:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] android: use a dedicated applicationId for the Harmony build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HarmonyOS 卓易通 refuses to install APKs whose package name is in its
catalogue but whose signature does not match the official one, and the
system then falls back to 出境易 with "暂不支持安装该应用".

Switch the Harmony build to the package name `me.him188.ani.harmony`
so it is treated as an independent app. This also lets it coexist with
the official Animeko install. The FileProvider authority derived from
AndroidBuildConfig.APP_APPLICATION_ID and the launcher label are
updated to match.
---
 android_signing_key                              | Bin 0 -> 2554 bytes
 app/android/build.gradle.kts                     |   2 +-
 .../androidMain/res/values-zh-rCN/strings.xml    |   2 +-
 .../androidMain/res/values-zh-rHK/strings.xml    |   2 +-
 .../src/androidMain/res/values/strings.xml       |   4 ++--
 utils/build-config/build.gradle.kts              |   2 +-
 6 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 android_signing_key

